"distress"},{"surface":"உழப்போள்","parts":[{"text":"உழப்போள்","lemma":"உழப்போள்","gloss":"she who suffers"}],"gloss":"she who suffers","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மல்லல்","parts":[{"text":"மல்லல்","lemma":"mallal","gloss":"abundance"}],"gloss":"abundance"},{"surface":"சிறப்ப","parts":[{"text":"சிறப்பு","lemma":"ciṟappu","gloss":"excellence"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to flourish"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செல்லா","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"cel","gloss":"go/diminish"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative adjectival participle"}],"gloss":"never-diminishing"},{"surface":"செல்வம்","parts":[{"text":"செல்வம்","lemma":"celvam","gloss":"wealth"}],"gloss":"wealth"},{"surface":"மிகுந்தனை","parts":[{"text":"மிகு","lemma":"miku","gloss":"abound"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"n","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"அனை","lemma":"aṉai","gloss":"second person singular suffix"}],"gloss":"you possess in abundance"},{"surface":"வல்லே","parts":[{"text":"வல்லே","lemma":"vallē","gloss":"quickly"}],"gloss":"quickly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விடுதல்","parts":[{"text":"விடு","lemma":"viṭu","gloss":"dismiss"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"tal","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"letting go"},{"surface":"வேண்டுவல்","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டு","lemma":"vēṇṭu","gloss":"request"},{"text":"வல்","lemma":"val","gloss":"first person singular suffix"}],"gloss":"I request"},{"surface":"அத்தை","parts":[{"text":"அத்தை","lemma":"attai","gloss":"expletive particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"படு","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"roaring"}],"gloss":"roaring"},{"surface":"திரை","parts":[{"text":"திரை","lemma":"tirai","gloss":"wave"}],"gloss":"waves"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீர்","parts":[{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"nīr","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"water"},{"surface":"சூழ்","parts":[{"text":"சூழ்","lemma":"cūḻ","gloss":"surround"}],"gloss":"surrounded"},{"surface":"நிலம்","parts":[{"text":"நிலம்","lemma":"nilam","gloss":"earth"}],"gloss":"earth"},{"surface":"வரை","parts":[{"text":"வரை","lemma":"varai","gloss":"limit"}],"gloss":"boundary"},{"surface":"உயர","parts":[{"text":"உயர்","lemma":"uyar","gloss":"rise"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to rise high"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சீர்","parts":[{"text":"சீர்","lemma":"cīr","gloss":"glory"}],"gloss":"glory"},{"surface":"கெழு","parts":[{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"keḻu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having"},{"surface":"விழு","parts":[{"text":"விழு","lemma":"viḻu","gloss":"great"}],"gloss":"great"},{"surface":"புகழ்","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்","lemma":"pukaḻ","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"},{"surface":"ஏத்துகம்","parts":[{"text":"ஏத்து","lemma":"ēttu","gloss":"praise"},{"text":"கம்","lemma":"kam","gloss":"first person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"we shall praise"},{"surface":"பல","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many things"}],"gloss":"many things"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"Like the bright rays of the dread-inspiring sun scorching / the withered-grass forest, making it sprout with roaring / thunderous clouds pouring rain, / the shriveled, weak body consumed by hunger, / withered because of not knowing the entry of cooked rice, / making the curved, striped intestines contract, so that cool / seasoned, rich meat-sauce and ghee-rich food / is served in small golden fine vessels, surrounding and seating them, / so that there is no deficiency for the singers' family, / easily bestowing rare golden ornaments, / Kumanan of good fame, who befriended his friends, / he of Mutiram hill with streets full of toddy, / 'If you go, he will grant greatly,' saying / those who speak many praises said, and very hastening, / my heart urging, I came, suffering from poverty. / My son with a tuft of hair in our house, many times, / sucked the empty breast without milk, and not obtaining it, / begging for gruel and cooked rice in turn, / seeing the coming pot inside empty, opening it and weeping, / telling of the fierce tiger and showing the moon, / she grieved, and saying 'think of your father / and show your dust-covered face,' and many things / asking without ceasing, in reality / she who suffers distress, so that her abundance flourishes, / you possess never-diminishing wealth in abundance, quickly / I request you to dismiss me, so that / as high as the boundary of the earth surrounded by water with roaring waves, / we shall praise your glorious, great fame in many ways.","translation":"Like the roaring thunder and pouring rain that make the withered forest sprout after being scorched by the bright rays of the fierce sun, you easily bestow rare golden ornaments so that the singers' families have no want, seating them around small golden plates to feed them ghee-rich rice with seasoned, rich meat sauce, making their shriveled intestines, which had shrunk from hunger, cool down. O Kumanan of great fame, who loves his friends, lord of Mutiram hill with streets rich in toddy! Hearing many praise you, saying, 'If you go to him, he will give you much,' I hastened here, urged by my heart, leaving behind my deep poverty. Back home, my little son with a tuft of hair sucked at his mother's dry, milkless breast, and getting nothing, begged for gruel and rice. Seeing him open the empty pots and weep, his mother tried to comfort him by telling stories of fierce tigers and pointing to the moon. Grieving, she said to him, 'Think of your father and show me your dust-covered face,' asking him many such things without ceasing. To make her life of waking misery flourish with abundance, you who possess inexhaustible wealth, please dismiss me quickly with gifts! So that, as high as the bounds of this earth surrounded by the roaring ocean, we may sing your glorious, great fame in many ways.","modern":"அச்சம் தரும் சூரியனின் ஒளிரும் கதிர்களால் காய்ந்துபோன புற்களைக் கொண்ட காடு, இடி முழக்கத்துடன் பெய்யும் மழையால் மீண்டும் தழைப்பது போல, பசியால் வாடிச் சுருங்கிய குடல்கள் குளிரும் வகையில், தாளித்த கொழுத்த இறைச்சிச் சாறும் நெய்யும் கலந்த உணவைச் சிறிய பொற்கலங்களில் சுற்றத்தாருக்குப் பகிர்ந்து அளித்து, பாணர்களின் சுற்றம் வறுமையின்றி வாழ அரிய பொன்னணிகளை எளிதாக வாரி வழங்கும் நல்ல புகழுடைய குமணன் முதிர மலைக்குத் தலைவன் ஆவான். 'அவனிடம் சென்றால் பெருங்கொடை தருவான்' என்று பலர் புகழக் கேட்டு, என் நெஞ்சம் தூண்ட நான் விரைந்து வந்தேன். என் இல்லத்தில், குடுமி வைத்த என் சிறு மகன் பாலில்லாத வறிய முலையைச் சுவைத்து ஏமாந்து, கஞ்சியும் சோறும் கேட்டு அழுது, வீட்டில் உள்ள பானைகளைத் திறந்து பார்த்து அவை காலியாக இருப்பதைக் கண்டு அழுதான். அவனது தாய், புலியைக் காட்டியும் நிலவைக் காட்டியும் சமாதானம் செய்ய முயன்றாள். மனம் நொந்து, 'உன் தந்தையை நினைத்துக்கொண்டு உன் தூசி படிந்த முகத்தைக் காட்டு' என்று பலவாறு கூறித் தேற்றினாள். நனவுலகில் இவ்வாறு துன்புறும் அவளது வறுமை நீங்கி வளம் பெருக, அழியாத செல்வத்தைக் கொண்டுள்ள நீ என்னை விரைவில் பரிசில் தந்து விடைபெறச் செய்ய வேண்டும். அலைகள் மோதும் கடல் சூழ்ந்த இந்நிலவுலகின் எல்லை வரை உயர, உனது சீர்மிகு விழுப்புகழை நாங்கள் பலவாறு ஏத்திப் பாடுவோம்.","explanation":"The poet Peruñcittiraṉār addresses Kumaṇaṉ, the generous chieftain of Mutiram hill, describing his extreme poverty and requesting a swift gift of wealth. He vividly depicts his starving family: his young son crying for food and opening empty pots, and his grieving wife trying to distract the child with stories of tigers and the moon while longing for her husband's return. The poet contrasts this domestic misery with Kumaṇaṉ's legendary generosity, comparing the chieftain's gifts to rain that revives a scorched forest. He asks Kumaṇaṉ to grant him wealth quickly so he can relieve his wife's suffering, promising to sing the patron's glory across the earth. Key words include 'வறுமுலை' (dry breast), 'அழக் கண்டு' (seeing him weep), and 'செல்லாச் செல்வம்' (never-diminishing wealth).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],